{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20","id":682603,"title":"questions about V20, W20 and M20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-29T20:18:39-07:00","id":682603,"title":"questions about V20, W20 and M20","content":"I know the 20th Anniversary product line is a version of cWOD that is set in the current decade, but the events of Time of Judgment never happened. Some people have said the 20th Anniversary books have no metaplot, but that can't be entirely true since the Mage books introduce a new faction (Threat Null) and one of the Werewolf books brings back Samuel Haight.<br /> <br /> Are any of the following metaplot events still part of V20/W20/M20 history: the Sixth Great Maelstrom, the Avatar Storm, the death of the Ravnos Antediluvian, the decimation of the Ravnos clan, the appearance of the Red Star, the death of Baba Yaga, the lifting of the Assamite's curse, the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla, the Stargazers leaving the Garou Nation, the destruction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, the birth of the Perfect Metis, the defeat of the Sabbat in New York, the Kuei-jin invasion of America and the destruction of the Anarch Free State?<br /> <br /> If the Sixth Great Maelstrom never happened in V20, do any of the books explain where the Harbingers of Skulls came from?<br /> <br /> Do any of the books mention the Imbued? Hunter the Reckoning has always been my favorite cWOD game and I've always wanted to know what they've been up to since 2004.<br /> <br /> Which characters from the old books get mentioned in the new books (besides Samuel Haight)?<br /> <br /> I've heard that By Night Studio's MET Vampire and Werewolf books take a different approach to continuity than the 20th Anniversary series. Which metaplot events are part of its history and which characters have been mentioned in these books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8145-voidmaster","user":"VoidMaster","date":". 09-29-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8145-voidmaster","name":"VoidMaster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:22:08-07:00","id":682615,"title":"","content":"The books in general try to be metaplot agnostic usually giving some small details on certain big events across the game line, but also giving some ideas about what to do if you decide to jettison the metaplot completely or alter to fit a number of needs. The only thing I can think of that has stuck is the Avatar Storm in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T23:32:04-07:00","id":682695,"title":"","content":"Like Nist said, the *20 books are very good about either making something multiple choice or settling on one as default and giving you the options in a sidebar or something. Let me do a quick dive in my copies to try to find some specific answers so you get a sense of how the books treat them.. From just the core books:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidMaster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20#post682603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Avatar Storm</div> </div> </div> </div>Full page and a half of options, nothing really nailed down as default.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the appearance of the Red Star </div> </div> </div>Not mentioned in any of the books.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Sixth Great Maelstrom </div> </div> </div>M20 defaults to it didn't happen but talks about options where it did happen and they rebuilt, it's still happening, etc.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the death of the Ravnos Antediluvian </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the decimation of the Ravnos clan </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the lifting of the Assamite's curse </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla </div> </div> </div>All four of these get a sidebar called &quot;canonical changes&quot; with Assamites and Ravnos getting a fuller description and Gangrel (and Malkavians) getting a mention for having changed over time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the destruction of the Tal'Mahe'Ra </div> </div> </div>They're still around, though hardly mentioned. They have an entire book on the way, IIRC.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the defeat of the Sabbat in New York </div> </div> </div>A cursory mention in an unrelated section defaults to New York being Sabbat controlled. Otherwise not mentioned.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the destruction of the Anarch Free State? </div> </div> </div>V20 mentions the Free State once, doesn't mention the destruction of it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Stargazers leaving the Garou Nation </div> </div> </div>Stargazers default to being in the Garou Nation in W20<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Kuei-jin invasion of America </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the death of Baba Yaga </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the birth of the Perfect Metis </div> </div> </div>Nothing about these three are mentioned.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Sixth Great Maelstrom never happened in V20, do any of the books explain where the Harbingers of Skulls came from? </div> </div> </div>V20 plays up their origin as a complete mystery.<br /> <br /> I hope you find these examples illuminating. The books have had to nail -some- stuff down as the default in that edition, and some of them might be slightly anachronistic from a metaplot standpoint - Malkavians using Dementation instead of Dominate while Assamites still being under their curse being the prime example I remember - but all of it is easily changeable and the books usually go out of their way to illustrate the different possibilities if it's an important story point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T00:52:09-07:00","id":682729,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 20 covers the Imbued in the corebook's &quot;Enemy&quot; chapter, and features one of them in Book of the Wyrm's Pentex chapter.<br /> <br /> On the Sixth Great Maelstrom, the impression I've picked up from what Rich Dansky has said is that Wraith 20 is set in a timeline where it hasn't happened. Orpheus get covered in a Wr20 appendix, but this is early Orpheus, before the events of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:06:13-07:00","id":682780,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to you could start from the beginning and play through the entire metaplot, only everything gets pushed forward 20 years and gehenna winds up happening in 2024.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:29:16-07:00","id":682794,"title":"","content":"In general, the books mention most of the metapolot and tell you it's optional. Some of them introduce some new events and ideas, but even those are optional. 20th anniversary is a version where you make your own metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T04:51:53-07:00","id":682972,"title":"","content":"M20 includes huge amounts of metaplot, but it's largely confined to sidebars (&quot;Future Fates&quot;). So the Avatar Storm is optional, for example, with various options on incorporating it into your game. These options are one or more versions of &quot;These things will happen&quot;, &quot;These things might happen&quot;, and &quot;These things may never happen&quot;. Future Fates sidebars cover things like the Ascension War, Doissietep's destruction, Heylel's return, the victory of the Technocratic paradigm, post-millennial developments like 9/11, the collapse of the Horizon realms, the Reckoning and the Week of Nightmares, the Avatar Storm, the Spirit-Nuke, the spread of cell-phones, the collapse of the Council of the Nine Traditions, the Sphinx and the Rogue Council, the reformed Technocracy, Nephandic infiltration of the Union, Threat Null, and the treachery of the Hollow Ones. These are covered in the first couple of hundred pages of the book. As you'll see, most of Mage's major metaplot developments are optional in M20, allowing the ST to set the dials to suit their own needs and desires <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T05:01:28-07:00","id":682997,"title":"","content":"Oh, and it also includes things like &quot;if you include this, you probably need to include this too, but you could also have this happen instead...&quot; and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:00:02-07:00","id":684341,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what everyone else has side but I must point out Threat Null did not originate in M20, it started in the completed Rev Ed Convention Books which are specifically set in a world where the Avatar Storm and early Rev Ed Metaplot but not the actual end of the world.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate CB first cryptically mentioned them when they talked about the VE and how they were always asking for more funding to deal with something they have called Threat Null. And then the VE CB revealed what Threat Null was, why the VE aren't telling their fellow Technocrats and why the Syndicate needs to shut up and give them whatever they want to deal with Threat Null.<br /> <br /> M20 only has the bullet points of Threat Null.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T17:29:47-07:00","id":685074,"title":"","content":"That said, some *20 books introduce their own completely new plot developments, though these seem to also be optional. V20 Rites of Blood, for instance, introduced the Montmartre Pact, which altered the established history of Clan Tremere so that, in order to enter the Camarilla in the first place, they had to free all their Gargoyles and swear off the creation of any more. This book also presented the first real write-up for the Inconnu, albeit stating flat-out that it was only one potential way of portraying them. The same chapter also presented an interpretation of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, with the same consideration.<br /> <br /> M20 is where a lot of developments happened...potentially. The transition from Disparates as disaffected Crafts to their own Alliance. The formal renaming of many Traditions, such as the Sons of Ether becoming the Society of Ether, etc. The Taftani now adapting to the modern day despite every other book on the subject making it clear they would rather die than accommodate the Consensus. The shifting of the Digital Web from Tron-esque to a fully realized HD world. Just a whole lot of little things that you can take or leave.<br /> <br /> While the 20th Anniversary editions all retain a fundamental metaplot agnosticism, each new book has the people at Onyx Path looking towards what sort of new things they can do with the systems and settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:03:20-07:00","id":685591,"title":"","content":"Do the character biographies in Children of the Revolution (and other *20 books that have character biographies) reveal anything about the metaplot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8145-voidmaster","name":"VoidMaster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T21:46:54-07:00","id":690884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidMaster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20#post682603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Are any of the following metaplot events still part of V20/W20/M20 history: the Kuei-jin invasion of America and the destruction of the Anarch Free State?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=682695#post682695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V20 mentions the Free State once, doesn't mention the destruction of it.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Actually, the Anarchs and where they are in the present are talked about in great length and detail in the V20 supplement, Anarchs Unbound. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The default setting that book uses is that Gehenna and the Kuei-Jin invasion has not happened. In this version of the setting, a new sub-faction of the Anarchs emerges called &quot;The Red Question&quot;, a hacktivist group of Anarchs (in the write-up, so pretty obvious allusions and parallels made to group like Anonymous). There existence was made known when they released a digital document called, well, &quot;Anarchs Unbound&quot;. Essentially meant to be a new and updated version of the original Anarch Manifesto. It also mentions how the Red Question was very instrumental in bringing Kindred society into the digital age, mostly due to the Camarilla and the Sabbat out of necessity so they don't keep getting thrashed by digital attacks. And because of that, i</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">t's said that the Thamauturgy Path of Technomancy originated and was developed by the Red Question. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And (more uncomfortably, at least for me) it's stated that the global 2008 recession was actually the doing of the Red Question, as a way to completely cripple the Camarilla's assets, and as a clear message telling the elders to back off from them. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">...yeah, needless to say I've chosen to ignore that particular plot point in my own Anarch V20 game. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There is a sidebar called &quot;Looking to the Future&quot; those essentially summarizes all the Revised events, specifically the ones that impacted the Anarchs in some way (including the aforementioned Kuei-Jin invasion, Tara's betrayal in San Diego, Justicar Petrodon's fate, and Baba Yaga). It doesn't really provide any suggestions on how to use or alter these events like Future Fates does in M20, save for just plugging them back in wholesale. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T16:33:51-07:00","id":691786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=690884#post690884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And (more uncomfortably, at least for me) it's stated that the global 2008 recession was actually the doing of the Red Question, as a way to completely cripple the Camarilla's assets, and as a clear message telling the elders to back off from them. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair the Syndicate blame themselves(and are blamed for) the recession as a Global Paradox effect for pushing too far. I am sure there's something in werewolf that says its Pentex's fault or some garou victory caused them to plummet etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T20:57:12-07:00","id":691958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=691786#post691786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair the Syndicate blame themselves(and are blamed for) the recession as a Global Paradox effect for pushing too far. I am sure there's something in werewolf that says its Pentex's fault or some garou victory caused them to plummet etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a much lighter implication on a rivalry between Murica, Ol'Mighty Dolla and Easy Credit, in that W20 Umbra describes though spirits as helping it to happen rather than causing it. Pentex itself only wishes that it could have caused it, and probably got burned at least a little, like everyone else. At least, before it most likely started sucking up bailout money to line the pockets of its upper management.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T21:26:01-07:00","id":691982,"title":"","content":"I've done some research about By Night Studio's metaplot. The Red Star faded away. Gehenna never happened or was somehow aborted. The Camarilla now acknowledges the existence of the Antediluvians. The Gangrel and Assamites are now part of the Camarilla. The Sabbat has lost a lot of its territory. The Giovanni have allied with the Setites. Hunters have become much more dangerous and are a much bigger problem for Kindred society.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if these hunters are meant to be the Society of Leopold, Project Twilight, the Imbued or some other faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8145-voidmaster","name":"VoidMaster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T21:42:11-07:00","id":691986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidMaster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=691982#post691982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done some research about By Night Studio's metaplot. The Red Star faded away. Gehenna never happened or was somehow aborted. The Camarilla now acknowledges the existence of the Antediluvians. The Gangrel and Assamites are now part of the Camarilla. The Sabbat has lost a lot of its territory. The Giovanni have allied with the Setites. Hunters have become much more dangerous and are a much bigger problem for Kindred society.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if these hunters are meant to be the Society of Leopold, Project Twilight, the Imbued or some other faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>BNS's new metaplot isn't the one that OPP is going to use for V4, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:14:32-07:00","id":692234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=691986#post691986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BNS's new metaplot isn't the one that OPP is going to use for V4, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Btw I've heard horrible stuff about BNS, could someone explain to me what are they actually doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T15:51:40-07:00","id":693062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=692234#post692234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Btw I've heard horrible stuff about BNS, could someone explain to me what are they actually doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>broadly building on Larpism<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T08:25:00-07:00","id":700869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=693062#post693062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> broadly building on Larpism</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In plain English, please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T13:17:05-07:00","id":701263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=700869#post700869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In plain English, please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tabletop is generally built around only 3 to 5 players existing and thus can be shaped as such. Larp generally has larger groups and thus puts more positions in the hands of players, also since alot of players have a better grasp of setting than your average neonate things end up getting consistantly revealed. so BNS Vampire for example has the Camarilla believe in the Antedeluvians but treat them as benign parental figures <br /> <br /> Sect base play tends to have things break up into periods of politicing in private rooms where no neutrals are allowed so the Independent clans end up spending a significant portion of their time play with eachother in these set ups so BNS formalizes this isn't the Independent alliance.<br /> <br /> Nobody is sure how to ever handle the Giovanni promise so they just drop it.<br /> <br /> Since games are generally one sect with some independents circling around most Gangrel pcs ignored the whole &quot;go independent&quot; thing since this basically just cuts them out of game play so BNS has them &quot;Returning&quot; to the cam.<br /> <br /> Since Anarchs are treated as a venue on par with Cam or Sabbat they have gained that level of status in setting as seperate setup.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alot of things that I'd say make no sense from a purely tabletop perspective but make perfect sense as building on years of how people end up playing Larp.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:58:17-07:00","id":701361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=701263#post701263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Tabletop is generally built around only 3 to 5 players existing and thus can be shaped as such. Larp generally has larger groups and thus puts more positions in the hands of players, also since alot of players have a better grasp of setting than your average neonate things end up getting consistantly revealed. so BNS Vampire for example has the Camarilla believe in the Antedeluvians but treat them as benign parental figures <br /> <br /> Sect base play tends to have things break up into periods of politicing in private rooms where no neutrals are allowed so the Independent clans end up spending a significant portion of their time play with eachother in these set ups so BNS formalizes this isn't the Independent alliance.<br /> <br /> Nobody is sure how to ever handle the Giovanni promise so they just drop it.<br /> <br /> Since games are generally one sect with some independents circling around most Gangrel pcs ignored the whole &amp;quot;go independent&amp;quot; thing since this basically just cuts them out of game play so BNS has them &amp;quot;Returning&amp;quot; to the cam.<br /> <br /> Since Anarchs are treated as a venue on par with Cam or Sabbat they have gained that level of status in setting as seperate setup.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alot of things that I'd say make no sense from a purely tabletop perspective but make perfect sense as building on years of how people end up playing Larp.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. And it sounds like it'd work for LARP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T01:30:39-07:00","id":701844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=701263#post701263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Larpisms<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeesh. So they decided to go towards gamist fidelity over setting fidelity. How do the larpers respond? I can see that the tabletop players would just go haywire, but it might be good to the larpers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T02:28:52-07:00","id":701877,"title":"","content":"Well the whole system is built on wonk, for wonk and by the wonk. The best example I can find is burning wrath is now a merit, let that sink in. Also the &quot;status&quot; system is very easy to abuse if you stack the pc correctly same with combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons! 10-15-2015, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T04:03:58-07:00","id":701928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=701844#post701844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeesh. So they decided to go towards gamist fidelity over setting fidelity. How do the larpers respond? I can see that the tabletop players would just go haywire, but it might be good to the larpers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say its Gameist fidelity vs acknowleding the setting that has developed in various larp organizations since official books went away, or even the breaks that began long before that when players got the reigns and took different choices than those driven by the writers. Its more a communal driven metaplot that way.<br /> <br /> Of course I play in a larp org that said &quot;fuck off&quot; to BNS and wants to use Onyx path stuff but can't because BNS has all rules for Larp stuff so they can only use old MET stuff, so I wouldn't say its an unqualified success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=701877#post701877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the whole system is built on wonk, for wonk and by the wonk. The best example I can find is burning wrath is now a merit, let that sink in. Also the &quot;status&quot; system is very easy to abuse if you stack the pc correctly same with combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Merits work differently in BNS than they do in tabletop. Merits are &quot;Special Snowflake points&quot; you get 7 of them period. You can use them to say be on a path, or be a Ravnos in a Cam game. Or have special powers of your clan. A number of clan only special tricks were made merits that way. I don't agree with the idea, but i don't think the combo disciplines that were converted to merits have been made easier to get that way.<br /> <br /> As for status I think its probably the best idea they had, but it really only shines in a larp setting, I would not use it for table top. But hte minigame of status works well in a game where there's a bunch of people who should be vying for status.<br /> <br /> As for stacking well that's just an issue that will always exist with using the RPS mechanic. SOmeone who has a pool of 6 fighting someone iwth a pool of 7 in tabletop has a much more even chance than 2/3s success the 7 will have vs the 6 with the RPS system. This is the price of simplicity.. however with the number of people I know who end up just using RPS apps I wonder if one couldn't run a straight v20 larp using dice rolling apps.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T17:58:56-07:00","id":702750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=701844#post701844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeesh. So they decided to go towards gamist fidelity over setting fidelity. How do the larpers respond? I can see that the tabletop players would just go haywire, but it might be good to the larpers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting fidelity is rather subjective, every individual player and ST imposes their own unique interpretation on the text. Genre has always been a collective construct filled with &quot;in my game&quot; exceptions. As to how LARPers have responded to it, some love it and some hate it. Big surprise. I have my criticisms of it personally but I lean much more toward the former than the latter. Its a breath of fresh air in a room that's been getting musty since around '99.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T18:20:05-07:00","id":702768,"title":"","content":"@ the OP<br /> <br /> Having just gotten the Backer version of Lore of the Clans, (and only reading through it still), it seems that they have begun to take some of that Setting Agnosticism and while not throw it out the window, find a much better/happier medium for including the metaplot and Revised Edition materials.<br /> <br /> For Example SPOILERS FOLLOW, in Revised, a very powerful Assamite Elder woke up, shattered the longstanding Tremere Curse the Clan, and the Assamites went through a few major changes, with, towards the end, large portions of the Clan leaving and trying to join the Camarilla. In V20, it backed way, way off from that, resetting it all to the 2nd Ed version, and ignoring Revised as much as possible.<br /> <br /> In Lore of the Clans, it sort of sets things up. It builds up that that individual is on the rise, and there is a small but growing group within the Clan that think he will wreck everything they have been working so hard to build, destroy the work they have put in to show not all Assamites are extremists, and there is talk about 2 of the Bloodlines leaving the Clan outright to join the Camarilla. All of this is set up to be just on the horizon, but not certain. It doesn't to go that way, but that's how it's starting to look, at least from inside the Clan and from the narrator's point of view.<br /> <br /> When I first got the book, I scanned through the Gangrel first, and I see some things in there that seem to do a similar job, but then I went back and started reading from the beginning. All in all, Lore of the Clans, so far, seems to be really redeeming the V20 line for the gripes I had about it's lack of metaplot elements. W20 did some minor improvements, but still stayed pretty neutral, but M20 was just outright amazing, including so many different things as possibilities from all across the metaplot(s) and editions, and Lore of t Clans seems to be going that extra step even further, but not forcing it for those that did not like any particular aspect(s), such as the Ravnos being nearly destroyed.<br /> <br /> So far, and this is just my still early impression, I highly recommend it. I also really hope they continue this trend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T19:32:22-07:00","id":702929,"title":"","content":"That reminds me, a hypothetical W4 is going to have to contend with the &quot;no more new changers are being born, only kinfolk&quot; part of W:tA end metaplot. It set up the whole &quot;all participants in the Apocalypse have been born already&quot; detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T04:50:05-07:00","id":703197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=701877#post701877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the whole system is built on wonk, for wonk and by the wonk. The best example I can find is burning wrath is now a merit, let that sink in. Also the &quot;status&quot; system is very easy to abuse if you stack the pc correctly same with combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems I made the right choice by sticking to Laws Of Night (Rev). And houseruling the crap out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T07:01:41-07:00","id":703371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/682603-questions-about-v20-w20-and-m20?p=703197#post703197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seems I made the right choice by sticking to Laws Of Night (Rev). And houseruling the crap out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly its the same problems you'd have with L:TNr, the whole damn trait stacking system and RPS simplicty leads to very odd mechanical issues. BNS doesn't fix this because well it still uses those things.<br /> <br /> Status is the best addition, I play a heavily house ruled LTNR revised and while I don't like merits as special snowflake points, the Return of beast traits and whole bunch of other choices they made(though I see why they made them) I do think the status system really works for Larp or at least camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","na